## Context
DECISIONS.md 2026-08-30 ratified the four-process pipeline: a shim extract
process over Zotero (owning the extracted-eventually-to-latest-extractor
bookkeeping), run-to-drain chunker and embedder workers, resident MCP query
servers. DESIGN.md still describes one background worker (P1) beside the
P0 servers. The ledger entry deliberately did not improvise the propagation:
§2.4 (background walk), §2.5 (conductor — "one worker" becomes "one of each
kind"), and §2.9 (process RAM arithmetic — run-to-drain means steady state
holds only the P0s) each need a careful rewrite, and §2.9's figures are
anchored in the figure guard, so the numbers move under the guard, not
around it.

## Relevant files
- `spec/DECISIONS.md` — the ruling (2026-08-30, four processes / shim extractor)
- `spec/DESIGN.md` §2.4, §2.5, §2.9 — the sections to align
- `bench/check_figures.py` — anchors on §2.9's RAM figures

## Actions
1. Rewrite §2.5's conductor for one-worker-of-each-kind, run-to-drain.
2. State the shim extract process and its bookkeeping in §2.4, with the
   byte-identical-transport fact (api-vs-cache-probe) and the pass-structure-
   through consequence.
3. Recompute §2.9's steady/transient RAM statements under the lifecycle;
   move anchors with the figures.

## Invariants
- No behaviour is designed here that the ruling did not state; open points
  (page-based segmenter) stay in Awaiting ratification.
- `make check` green throughout; every moved figure keeps an anchor.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] The three sections state the four-process model and cite the ruling
- [ ] No document still describes chunk+embed as one worker
- [ ] Figure guard green with the moved RAM figures
